    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We have developed a model for evaluating vertical fault continuity in layered rock, and have applied this model to an oil field development project in the Berkine Basin, Algeria. Seismic images from the Berkine Basin suggest that some fault sets cut through the entire stratigraphic section, while other fault sets are localized in specific lithologies. From our model, we have predicted this behavior and have developed quantitative criteria for determining when faults should be extended through multiple stratigraphic intervals.",
